WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.524
Your data model, as a diagram, saved as plain files in your repo.

2
00:00:04.574 --> 00:00:07.061
No AI, and nothing to configure.

3
00:00:07.511 --> 00:00:12.035
Install ERD Studio, and open the folder your data model lives in.

4
00:00:12.085 --> 00:00:14.399
The Get started guide opens by itself.

5
00:00:14.849 --> 00:00:17.417
Click New Diagram, and give it a name.

6
00:00:20.049 --> 00:00:22.684
Add a table, with starter columns if you like.

7
00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:25.655
Add another, then link the two with a relationship.

8
00:00:29.049 --> 00:00:34.667
Each table is a plain DBML file in your repo, to commit and review like code.

9
00:00:35.449 --> 00:00:39.543
Already have DBML? Import it, and export back any time.

10
00:00:40.649 --> 00:00:43.501
Want grain, keys and the why behind each table?

11
00:00:43.551 --> 00:00:48.968
Click Set Up My AI Helper, then type /erd-studio-setup in your assistant.

12
00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:54.523
ERD Studio is free. Install it, and draw your data model today.
